Demonstrating wait() and waitpid().

Explanation:

Function - Purpose
fork() - Creates a child process.
wait() - Makes the parent wait until any child process terminates.
waitpid() - Makes the parent wait for a specific child process.
sleep() - Pauses execution for a specified number of seconds.


Important concepts:

wait(NULL) – Waits for any child process to finish.
waitpid(pid, NULL, 0) – Waits for the child whose PID is stored in pid.
NULL – Indicates that the exit status is not being collected.
0 – Uses the default blocking behaviour of waitpid().
